### Variables
@host = http://localhost:5242
@customerId = 1
@storeId = 1
@addressId = 1
@orderId = 1

### 1. Create a Customer
POST {{host}}/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Developer",
  "lastName": "Antigravity",
  "email": "dev.antigravity@wasil.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0798765432"
}

### 2. Add an Address for the Customer
POST {{host}}/api/v1/customers/{{customerId}}/addresses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "street": "123 Agent Lane",
  "city": "Amman",
  "zipCode": "11190",
}

### 3. List Customer Addresses
GET {{host}}/api/v1/customers/{{customerId}}/addresses

### 4. List Stores
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stores?name=Market&page=1&pageSize=5

### 5. Search Products (Catalog)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?storeId={{storeId}}&text=milk&page=1&pageSize=5

### 6. Store Details (With Product Count)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stores/{{storeId}}

### 7. Place an Order
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "storeId": {{storeId}},
  "addressId": {{addressId}},
  "paymentMethod": 0,
  "lines": [
    {
      "productId": 1,
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### 8. Get Order Details
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

### 9. Get Customer Order History
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/customer/{{customerId}}?page=1&pageSize=5

### 10. Update Order Status (Pending -> Accepted)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 1
}

### 11. Get Store Dashboard
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/dashboard/{{storeId}}
